title: '2. One mind writes the plan: the owner of the territory where its hardest decision lies.'
pid: ed1da9a0-8972-4e28-9e0a-ca5f269588f8
body: |2-
  One author, never two in turns or in parallel: a plan is where the
  decisions become explicit, and two authors make two sets of them.
  The hardest decision is usually the one-way door from step 1. The
  author reads the other territories' maps in their graphs. Where a
  map does not answer, it writes the question in its 'to Claude', and
  Top sends that owner a short mission that answers only that.
  Top does not write plans: Top does not read code, and costs most.
  If no territory holds the hardest decision (a request about how the
  team works, say), Top names the author by the way of seeing it most needs.
  Rests on: read (Cognition: one thread of decisions; a helper that
  only answers a question is safe). Ours: the choice of owner, and
  that Top does not author, departing from Anthropic's research
  system, where the lead plans. ? (unsure: a border inside one function.)
